    "question": {
      ":question/id": "12086c85-5ce0-525b-9d90-1d212d477ac8",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $B?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $4$ times the first row to the third row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $5$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 4+(4)(4) & -8+(4)(-8) & 9+(4)(8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 20 & -40 & 41\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 8+(5)(4) & -2+(5)(-8) & 8+(5)(8) \\\\ 20 & -40 & 41\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 28 & -42 & 48 \\\\ 20 & -40 & 41\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
