    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2578b9c7-350b-563f-9dc8-b49ba72556cb",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $-5$ times the second row to the third row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 7+(-5)(1) & -1+(-5)(2) & 1+(-5)(8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -11 & -39\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-4+(2)(1) & -4+(2)(2) & 5+(2)(8) \\\\ 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -11 & -39\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 21 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -11 & -39\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
